{"type":"text","timestamp":1794535643257,"sessionID":"ses_e2d59c360ffeZZjXvmuyO2sn3H","part":{"id":"prt_1d2a8cb0b002lzvelZXy7wQB9X","sessionID":"ses_e2d59c360ffeZZjXvmuyO2sn3H","messageID":"msg_1d2a8b944001yvyoCDvs3TBV1Q","type":"text","text":"T023 done. Edited only `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml`: inserted the embedder leg directly after the advisor leg, and changed both \"five read-only legs\" phrases in `purpose` and `action` to \"six\".\n\nVerify output, run from the repo root:\n\n```\n$ rg -n \"Leg embedder\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n58:    - \"Leg embedder: run node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_status --workspace-root \\\"$PWD\\\" --include-semantic-health true --format json --timeout-ms 1500 --warm-only. Exit 75 is SKIP, as for the advisor leg, because the daemon is not running. Exit 0 with data.semanticLaneHealth.laneEnabled true and data.semanticLaneHealth.commandVectorCoverage.embedded above 0 is PASS. Any other result is DEGRADED, never FAIL, with repair /doctor:skill-advisor embedder.\"\nexit 0\n\n$ rg -n \"five read-only\" .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup.yaml\n(no output)\nexit 1\n```\n\nThe second check is a real absence, not a broken pattern: the same regex matches `setup.md:62` and `doctor-setup-presentation.txt:19`. `python3 -c 'import yaml; ...'` also parses the file cleanly (11 steps). The diff is confined to the one named file, and the checkbox is untouched.\n\nTwo files outside my scope still say the setup route has five legs, so they will contradict the YAML: `.skilled/commands/doctor/setup.md:62` and `.skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt:19`. The presentation file is T024's, and T024 only asks for the leg row and target row, so someone should decide whether the \"five\" wording there is covered. Nothing else was left undone.","time":{"start":1794535639819,"end":1794535643257}}}
